__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
*.log
venv/

# ─── `data/` is BOTH a source package and the bots' state directory ─────────
#
# C6. The repository ROOT .gitignore carries a bare `data/` rule — added for the
# main Valquo tree's licensed Sharadar exports, which genuinely must never be
# committed. A gitignore pattern whose only slash is the trailing one matches at
# EVERY depth, so that rule also excluded `options-bot/quant_bots/data/` when
# this subproject was added later.
#
# The consequence was not cosmetic. `options/orchestrator/jobs.py`,
# `options/screener/screener.py` and `options/scripts/screen.py` all import from
# `data` / `data.earnings`, and NONE of those source files is tracked in git. On
# a clean clone `cd options && python -m unittest discover` collects 53 of 181
# tests and fails with 14x `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'data'` — and
# `deploy/deploy.sh` treats a failing options suite as fatal and aborts BEFORE
# restarting any service. That is a mechanical explanation for why three fixed
# bugs sat in the repository undeployed: the git deploy path could not complete.
# The zip flow deploy.sh replaced carried `data/` fine, because a zip does not
# consult .gitignore.
#
# `!data/` re-includes the directory (a deeper .gitignore wins over a shallower
# one, and the directory itself must be un-excluded before anything inside it
# can be), and each state subdirectory is then re-ignored BY NAME. Do not
# collapse this back to a bare `data/` — the source package would disappear
# again and the failure mode is silent until a deploy.
!data/
data/cache/
data/state/
data/journal/
data/sim/
data/reports/
data/backtest/
